# Data files are committed directly as normal Git objects.
#
# Git LFS was set up early on, but the only dataset here
# (data/raw/broadband_customers.csv) is about 150 KB and was committed as a plain
# file, so the LFS rules only produced "should have been a pointer" warnings on
# clone. At this size plain Git is the simpler choice. If a large dataset is
# added later, track that file type with `git lfs track`.

# Keep line endings consistent across Windows and Linux.
* text=auto
